    "created_at": "2022-07-21T03:57:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-21T03:57:56Z",
    "body": "zsh [does not expand tilde inside of double quotes](https://unix.stackexchange.com/questions/151850/why-doesnt-the-tilde-expand-inside-double-quotes). You can check [this post](https://unix.stackexchange.com/questions/146671/does-always-equal-home/146697#146697) for more details.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like a solution where it's expanded, you could try using `$HOME`, e.g. \r\n\r\n```\r\nexport STARSHIP_CONFIG=\"$HOME/.config/starship/config.toml\"\r\n```",
